{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"foilable-soppy-flyingfox","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`tests/unit/workflow/test_executor_tripwire.py:20-93` checks imports and prose but cannot detect a hand-written retry loop. ADR 0065 requires the synchronous workflow engine to invoke an effectful step once rather than scheduling bespoke retries.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a behavioral tripwire whose effectful step increments an external observation and raises. Execute it through the production interpreter and assert one invocation, serial ordering, and immediate propagation. Retain current source/import checks as secondary architecture diagnostics.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_executor_tripwire.py`\n- existing workflow test fixtures needed to execute the real interpreter\n\n## Testing\n\nCover a raising effectful step, an ordinary successful sequence, and a later step that must remain uncalled after failure.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A raising effectful step is observed exactly once through the production workflow runtime.\n- [ ] No downstream step runs after the injected failure and execution remains serial.\n- [ ] The successful multi-step control still executes each step once in declared order.\n- [ ] Existing import/prose tripwires remain as secondary diagnostics and the focused workflow suite passes.","id":"90e2-6d13-ecfb-4131","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","priority":2,"tags":["janitor","workflow","oracle","rp06"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Add a behavioral single-invocation workflow oracle"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788311191661314001,"uuid":"d92f91b5-9d52-4524-b153-350c91ccdb55"}